dist/
*.log
# ...except a run's record filed in the docs tree. 06_docs IS the durable place;
# a record there that git ignores looks filed and is not (0.14.1 hygiene).
!06_docs/**/*.log
.DS_Store
.claude/
.a2dh/
coverage.out
*.test
*.prof

# Local development harness — not part of the public project
_a2dh/
.a2dh*
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
.github/copilot-instructions.md

# machine-local go-studs patches the sync applies first (the public-tree wording scrub stays out of the public tree)
third_party/go-studs/.local/

# the exposure scan's optional LOCAL identifier supplement (never tracked)
scripts/quality/exposure-identities.local.txt

# TOOL BINARIES BUILT IN THE ROOT. `go build ./tools/<x>/` drops the binary in
# the working directory, and the project rule is that every binary goes to
# ./dist/. The tools are RUN with `go run`; nothing needs a built copy.
#
# A DENYLIST HERE IS NOT THE GUARD, and this file is the evidence. Two tool
# binaries reached commits while these lines stood — the second AFTER this
# paragraph was written, by an author who had read it. A list of names cannot
# cover a tool that does not exist yet, so the standing check is
# `TestNoTrackedBinaries` in cmd/watchpost: it asks what the INDEX holds, not
# what someone remembered to name. These entries keep the working tree tidy.
/dupes
/wires
/slope
/geotrim
/nwrtable
/alertrec
/authoring
/treelock
